---
import { HANDICAP_PUBLISHED } from '../../../data/handicapSources';
import ArticlePage from '../../../components/ArticlePage.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../../utils/paths';
import { HANDICAP_SELECTION_WINDOW, MIN_HANDICAP_ROUNDS, estimateHandicap, formatHandicap, roundedDifferential } from '../../../utils/handicap';
import { calculate, parseRound } from '../../../utils/handicapCalculator';
import type { HandicapRound, RoundInput } from '../../../types/handicap';
import { HANDICAP_GUIDE_UPDATED, USGA_NET_DOUBLE_BOGEY_URL, WA_GOLF_DIFFERENTIAL_URL, ENGLAND_GOLF_INDEX_URL } from '../../../data/whsSources';
import { HANDICAP_CALLS, HANDICAP_TARGET } from '../../../data/storeCalls';

const INITIAL_RESULT: string = calculate([]).message;

const EXAMPLE_ROUNDS: readonly RoundInput[] = [
  { score: '90', rating: '72.0', slope: '113' },
  { score: '92', rating: '72.0', slope: '113' },
  { score: '94', rating: '72.0', slope: '113' },
];

function exampleRound(input: RoundInput): HandicapRound {
  const round = parseRound(input);
  if (round === null) throw new Error(`Invalid example round: ${JSON.stringify(input)}`);
  return round;
}

function differentialText(input: RoundInput): string {
  return roundedDifferential(exampleRound(input)).toFixed(1);
}

function exampleResult(): string {
  const estimate = estimateHandicap(EXAMPLE_ROUNDS.map(exampleRound));
  if (estimate.kind !== 'estimate') throw new Error('The example needs enough rounds for an estimate');
  return formatHandicap(estimate.value);
}

const EXAMPLE_RESULT: string = exampleResult();

---
<ArticlePage
  pageTitle="Golf Handicap Calculator: 18-Hole Estimate | SundayStroke"
  description="Estimate your golf handicap from 3 to 20 eighteen-hole rounds using your scores, course ratings and slopes. See a worked example and what the calculator leaves out."
  eyebrow="Tool · Golf handicap"
  heading="Golf handicap calculator"
  dates={{ published: HANDICAP_PUBLISHED, modified: HANDICAP_GUIDE_UPDATED }}
  banner={HANDICAP_TARGET}
  calls={HANDICAP_CALLS}
>
  <p>
    Enter your 18-hole rounds, newest first. For each one you need three numbers from the scorecard: your adjusted gross score,
    the course rating and the slope rating of the tees you played. You need at least {MIN_HANDICAP_ROUNDS} rounds; the newest
    {HANDICAP_SELECTION_WINDOW} count. The result updates as you type.
  </p>
  <form class="not-prose my-8 flex flex-col gap-4" id="handicap-form" data-max-rows={HANDICAP_SELECTION_WINDOW}>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-sm text-mist" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>Adjusted gross score</span>
      <span>Course Rating</span>
      <span>Slope Rating</span>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3" id="handicap-rows">
      {Array.from({ length: MIN_HANDICAP_ROUNDS }, (_, index) => (
        <fieldset class="handicap-row grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
          <legend class="sr-only">Round {index + 1}</legend>
          <input class="ss-card px-3 py-3 text-body-lg text-ice" name="score" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="Adj. gross" aria-label={`Round ${index + 1} adjusted gross score`} />
          <input class="ss-card px-3 py-3 text-body-lg text-ice" name="rating" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="Rating" aria-label={`Round ${index + 1} course rating`} />
          <input class="ss-card px-3 py-3 text-body-lg text-ice" name="slope" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="Slope" aria-label={`Round ${index + 1} slope`} />
        </fieldset>
      ))}
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="ss-btn ss-btn--secondary self-start" id="add-round">Add round</button>
    <output class="ss-card block p-6 text-title-2 text-ice" id="handicap-result" aria-live="polite">{INITIAL_RESULT}</output>
  </form>

  <h2>How to fill it in</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Adjusted gross score:</strong> your adjusted gross score for the round, as a whole number. Before you type it, cap any bad hole at net double bogey (par + 2 + the strokes you get on that hole), or at par + 5 if you don't have a handicap yet (<a href={USGA_NET_DOUBLE_BOGEY_URL}>USGA Rule 3.1</a>). The calculator only sees the total, so it can't apply the cap for you.</li>
    <li><strong>Rating:</strong> the course rating of your tees, such as 72.0 or 69.4. A comma works too.</li>
    <li><strong>Slope:</strong> the slope rating of your tees, a whole number from 55 to 155. A Slope Rating of 113 represents standard relative difficulty.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Add round</strong> for each extra round, up to {HANDICAP_SELECTION_WINDOW}. Put your newest round at the top.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Blank rows are ignored. If a row you started has a missing number, text, a decimal score or a slope outside 55 to 155, the
    calculator names that round and shows no estimate until you fix it or clear it, so you never get a result that quietly left a
    round out.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to find the course rating and slope</h2>
  <p>
    Most scorecards print a rating and a slope next to each set of tees, often as two numbers like "71.5 / 125". Clubs also list
    them on their website and in the pro shop. Use the numbers for the tees you actually played: the same course can be rated 74.1
    from the back and 69.0 from the front. Golf GPS reads them for you when you choose your tee at the start of a round.
  </p>

  <h2>Try a three-round example</h2>
  <p>Enter these three rounds, all from tees with a course rating of 72.0 and a slope of 113:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Round</th><th>Adjusted gross score</th><th>Rating</th><th>Slope</th><th>Differential</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {EXAMPLE_ROUNDS.map((round, index) => (
        <tr><td>{index + 1}</td><td>{round.score}</td><td>{round.rating}</td><td>{round.slope}</td><td>{differentialText(round)}</td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    On a slope of 113 each differential is simply the score minus the rating: 18.0, 20.0 and 22.0
    (<a href={WA_GOLF_DIFFERENTIAL_URL}>the score differential formula</a>). With three rounds, the World Handicap System uses the
    lowest one and takes 2.0 off (<a href={ENGLAND_GOLF_INDEX_URL}>England Golf: fewer than 20 scores</a>), so 18.0 − 2.0 gives
    <strong>{EXAMPLE_RESULT}</strong>. That is an illustrative estimate, not an official index.
  </p>

  <h2>Understand your result</h2>
  <p>
    For each round, the calculator assumes the playing conditions calculation (PCC) is 0.0 and works out an 18-hole score
    differential, (113 ÷ slope) × (score − rating), rounded to one decimal. It then picks your lowest differentials by the World
    Handicap System's table for 3 to 20 rounds, averages them, applies the table's adjustment for 3, 4 or 6 rounds, and rounds the
    estimate to one decimal. With 20 rounds it averages your lowest 8. Caps and exceptional-score reductions are not included. The
    result can't go above 54.0, and a result below zero shows as a plus handicap such as +1.5. The <a href={sitePath('/golf-handicap/')}>full handicap guide</a> explains each step with examples.
  </p>

  <h2>What this calculator doesn't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It accepts 18-hole rounds only. It doesn't combine nine-hole scores with an expected score.</li>
    <li>It assumes the playing conditions calculation (PCC) was 0.0 on every day.</li>
    <li>It doesn't apply the soft cap, the hard cap or the exceptional score reduction, because it doesn't know your handicap history.</li>
    <li>It doesn't cap hole scores; you enter a total that is already adjusted.</li>
    <li>It doesn't issue or replace an official Handicap Index. For that, join a golf club or your national association.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <h3>Can I enter nine-hole scores?</h3>
  <p>No. This calculator accepts 18-hole rounds only. Golf GPS Pro does count nine-hole rounds in its estimate.</p>
  <h3>Does it give me an official handicap?</h3>
  <p>No. This calculator produces an illustrative estimate from the adjusted totals you enter. Golf GPS Pro applies its own hole-score limit and also counts nine-hole rounds, so the two estimates can differ.</p>
  <h3>Why is my result lower than my average score over the rating?</h3>
  <p>Because a handicap uses your lowest differentials, not all of them. It reflects your better rounds rather than your average.</p>
  <h3>Do you keep my scores?</h3>
  <p>No. The calculation runs in your browser and nothing you type is sent anywhere.</p>
</ArticlePage>

<script>
  import '../../../scripts/handicapCalculatorForm';
</script>
